& [LangSOPInitialWorkflow] is the expanded platform subject for compiling SOP-governed reasoning duties into operational runtime layers
  + [root_purpose] is reduce repeated model-side SOP execution by turning stable duties into inspectable operators, LangGraph subgraphs, validators, and surface projections
  + [semantic_source_layer] is SOP source, proof, reconsideration, and authority material
  + [authority_kernel] is the durable typed record system that preserves source logs, narrative claims, authority artifacts, support records, work packets, completion reviews, and freshness state
  + [procedural_layer] is LangGraph workflow execution over kernel records
  + [projection_layer] is IRC, Matrix, Codex, terminal, web dashboard, Langflow, and other conversation or visualization surfaces
  + [model_judgment_layer] is the human or AI reasoning layer used when operators cannot mechanically decide a question
  + [soft_wire_layer] is SOP retained as the semantic debugging and reconsideration system after stable duties are compiled

  = must: compile only stable, frequent, mechanically checkable SOP duties
  = must: keep truth-bearing records outside LangGraph checkpoints
  = must: let LangGraph execute procedural shape without becoming the authority model
  = must: let existing surface tools consume and display kernel state without owning truth
  = must: return to SOP for meaning, ambiguity, authority changes, failed proof interpretation, and semantic repair
  = must: preserve blocked objectives inside the capability field even when they are not sliceable
  - never: treat a chat surface, Langflow flow, LangGraph checkpoint, or work packet as the source of truth by itself

## Layer Model

& [SemanticProofLayer] is the SOP-first layer
  + [owned_material] is source documents, canonical specifications, proof traces, narrative authorities, reconsideration records, and invalidation rules
  + [operational_role] is define meaning, authority, constraints, and appeal paths
  + [runtime_role] is act as soft-wire debugging and reprocessing source when compiled operators fail, drift, or become stale

  = must: preserve original source language and source hashes
  = must: carry SJS satisfaction signatures for canonical specifications
  = must: retain retired or superseded authority as trace

& [AuthorityKernelLayer] is the typed collaboration record layer
  + [owned_material] is source_log, narrative_node, understanding_anchor, authority_artifact, capability_node, requirement_record, support_record, coordination_claim, work_packet, completion_review, citation_ref, stale_projection, and proof_result
  + [operational_role] is store current and historical truth-bearing records with provenance and freshness rules
  + [runtime_role] is provide stable data to LangGraph nodes, dashboards, agents, and review surfaces

  = must: distinguish source data from derived projections
  = must: preserve lineage from every projection to its source data
  = must: expose stale, blocked, unsupported, and contradicted state instead of smoothing it away

& [LangGraphProcedureLayer] is the compiled execution layer
  + [owned_material] is subgraph definitions, node contracts, checkpoint state, interrupt points, and procedural transitions
  + [operational_role] is execute stable ReasoningFramework procedures over typed kernel records
  + [runtime_role] is reduce repeated manual SOP interpretation during ordinary workflow cycles

  = must: treat each graph node as an operator over kernel records
  = must: checkpoint execution state without claiming checkpoint state is authority
  = must: use human or model interrupts when judgment is required

& [SurfaceProjectionLayer] is the multi-surface collaboration layer
  + [owned_material] is views, adapters, rendered conversation surfaces, manager dashboards, worker packets, Langflow prototypes, IRC rooms, Matrix rooms, Codex prompts, terminal summaries, and web interfaces
  + [operational_role] is create and display collaboration state through usable interfaces

  = must: preserve projection lineage to kernel records
  = must: allow surfaces to submit events through validated operators
  - never: let a surface rewrite canonical authority without an authority operator

## Whole-Field Development Model

& [WholeFieldDevelopmentPlanning] is the upgraded planning model that bakes the entire capability field before creating on-demand work packets
  + [capability_field] is the whole graph of desired, supported, blocked, deferred, and verified capabilities
  + [capability_node] is one meaningful capability or objective in the field
  + [blocked_objective] is a capability_node that belongs in the field but cannot yet become a work packet
  + [readiness_projection] is the derived view of which capability nodes can be packetized now
  + [work_packet] is a generated view over one or more capability nodes under current readiness rules
  + [completion_review] is the between-packet review that updates support, requirements, freshness, and narrative state

  = must: model the whole intended capability field before optimizing for worker-sized slices
  = must: keep blocked objectives visible with blocker reasons and resolution conditions
  = must: generate work packets on demand from authority, support, dependency, ownership, risk, and verification conditions
  = must: review completed packets for support_delta and requirement_delta before generating the next packet

| [CapabilityReadiness] is (desired | source_preserved | specified | supported | blocked | deferred | ready_to_packetize | assigned | implemented | verified | stale | superseded | contradicted)
| [PacketKind] is (research | specification | architecture | implementation | fixture | proof | ledger_update | adapter | review | rendezvous | blocker_resolution | operations)
| [AuthorityState] is (source_only | narrative_projection | accepted_decision | signed_sjs | proof_backed | stale_projection | contradicted | invalidated | human_override)

& [CapabilityNode] is the central whole-field planning unit
  + [capability_id] is a stable identifier
  + [capability_name] is a human-readable subject name
  + [purpose] is why the capability exists
  + [authority_state] is one AuthorityState value
  + [readiness_state] is one CapabilityReadiness value
  + [requirement_set] is the atomic obligations for the capability
  + [dependency_set] is upstream capabilities, artifacts, decisions, proofs, tools, or environment requirements
  + [support_set] is support records that make implementation or proof possible
  + [blocker_set] is blockers that prevent packetization
  + [proof_route] is the verification path for completion claims
  + [packetization_rule] is the condition that permits generating work_packet records
  + [narrative_anchor_set] is the narrative and understanding material that explains context

  = must: be stored separately from generated work packets
  = must: preserve authority_state and readiness_state independently
  = must: allow blocked capability nodes to remain first-class planning material

## Candidate Compiled Duties

& [CompiledDutyCandidateSet] is the first group of SOP duties likely to become operators or LangGraph nodes
  + [signature_validation] is checking whether a specification has a valid SJS satisfaction signature and lineage
  + [inbox_check] is checking coordination mailbox directories and emitting unread-message events
  + [dirty_surface_classification] is classifying workspace changes as owned, foreign, mixed, unknown, or generated
  + [coordination_claim_overlap] is comparing active claims and overlap keys for conflicts
  + [support_readiness_recompute] is deriving readiness from requirements, support, gaps, proofs, and freshness rules
  + [work_packet_generation] is producing worker-ready packet records from ready capability nodes
  + [completion_delta_review] is deriving support_delta, requirement_delta, stale projections, and next frontiers after completed work
  + [stale_projection_detection] is checking whether mutable sources invalidated derived projections
  + [citation_index_update] is promoting citation candidates into durable citation references

  = must: start with operators whose inputs, outputs, and verification oracles can be defined
  = must: record operator traces so runtime behavior can be audited against SOP authority

& [SOPFirstDutySet] is the set of duties that should remain semantic-first until stable enough to compile
  + [new_architecture] is broad or high-consequence design work
  + [new_specification_source] is dictated or imported specification material that needs preservation and SJS processing
  + [ambiguous_identity] is a subject boundary or natural-key question requiring delineation
  + [authority_conflict] is contradiction between source, signature, proof, or user instruction
  + [requirement_mutation] is a change to the meaning or dependency shape of a requirement
  + [major_reroute] is a changed implementation route with narrative and proof implications
  + [failed_proof_interpretation] is proof failure that cannot be mechanically classified
  + [narrative_reframing] is a change in story meaning, readiness, or cross-subject feedback

  = must: route these duties through SOP and model/human judgment before compiling

## Candidate LangGraph Shape

& [WholeFieldPlannerGraph] is the initial LangGraph procedural shape for LangSOP
  + [SourceIntakeNode] preserves dictated or imported source material
  + [DelineationNode] forms stable subject boundaries
  + [CapabilityFieldNode] creates or updates capability_node records
  + [DataDesignNode] derives conceptual, logical, and physical data model obligations
  + [RequirementSupportNode] extracts requirements, dependencies, support, and gaps
  + [AuthorityClassificationNode] classifies source-only, signed, proof-backed, stale, contradicted, or invalid authority states
  + [ReadinessProjectionNode] recomputes packetization readiness
  + [WorkPacketGeneratorNode] emits candidate work packets
  + [HumanReviewInterrupt] pauses for human approval when authority, ambiguity, or risk requires it
  + [DispatchNode] assigns or publishes work packets
  + [CompletionReviewNode] inspects completed work for deltas, faults, and stale state
  + [NarrativeUpdateNode] records narrative arcs, reentry material, and unresolved items
  + [SJSUpdateNode] creates or updates SJS artifacts when authority changes
  + [RecomputeReadinessNode] refreshes readiness after deltas

  = must: keep graph state minimal enough to resume execution
  = must: store truth-bearing records in the authority kernel
  = must: expose interrupts for authority changes and unresolved ambiguity

## Development Stages

& [LangSOPDevelopmentStages] is the staged plan for implementation
  + [stage_0_source_intake] is source preservation, manifest creation, and initial SJS processing
  + [stage_1_capability_field_schema] is defining capability_node, requirement_record, support_record, authority_artifact, and work_packet schemas
  + [stage_2_kernel_storage] is selecting and implementing the first durable kernel storage representation
  + [stage_3_operator_contracts] is defining compiled-duty operator inputs, outputs, traces, and proof routes
  + [stage_4_langgraph_proof_of_shape] is implementing the first LangGraph workflow over kernel records
  + [stage_5_surface_projection] is producing manager, worker, narrative, and debugging views from kernel state
  + [stage_6_reasoningframework_duty_compilation] is compiling existing SOP duties into tested operators incrementally
  + [stage_7_operations_manager] is adding machine/job/resource supervision for the target Ryzen 9 RTX 5090 environment

  = must: keep stage_0 through stage_3 mostly architecture and authority work
  = must: avoid implementing broad operations management before kernel authority and packetization semantics are stable
  = should: make stages after stage_3 produce small Spark-suitable implementation packets where possible

## Model Routing

& [LangSOPModelRouting] is the budget-aware model policy for this project
  + [requires_deeper_reasoning] is architecture, authority kernel design, SOP-to-LangGraph compilation boundary, ambiguous data identity, major reroutes, and operations-manager safety policy
  + [spark_suitable] is bounded schema implementation, validators, tests, fixtures, proof refreshes, adapter nodes, ledger updates, and template generation after contracts stabilize

  = must: mark each generated work packet as Spark-suitable or requiring deeper reasoning
  = must: escalate Spark-suitable work back to deeper reasoning when a design fork, ambiguous failure, or authority conflict appears

## SJS Processing Trace

& [SJSProcessingTrace: LangSOPInitialWorkflow] is the seven-fold processing trace for this initial specification
  + [fold_1_subject] is LangSOP is a platform for compiling stable SOP duties into operational graph and kernel layers, not a replacement for SOP authority
  + [fold_2_boundary] is SOP, kernel, LangGraph, surfaces, and model judgment have distinct responsibilities
  + [fold_3_data_design] is capability_node, source_log, narrative_node, authority_artifact, support_record, work_packet, completion_review, and readiness_projection are the first core data subjects
  + [fold_4_governance] is source preservation and SJS signatures remain stronger than generated projections or graph checkpoints
  + [fold_5_solution_shape] is begin with SOP specifications and schemas before implementing runtime graph execution
  + [fold_6_fault_review] is over-compiling semantic duties, treating LangGraph state as authority, hiding blocked objectives, and skipping completion review are primary workflow faults
  + [fold_7_phase_lock] is the subject is stable enough for initial canonical specification and staged development, with unresolved implementation choices preserved as open questions
  + [exhaustion_state] is phase_locked_for_initial_planning_not_runtime_complete

  = must: promote only the canonical specification after satisfaction signature validation
  = must: preserve this exploded file as derivation trace
